# Unit cube for BHS test task 01 (Quake RTX on Apple Metal)
# 24 vertices (4 per face, so every face has its own UVs and normal), 12 triangles.
# Coordinates: right-handed, Y up, cube spans [-0.5, 0.5]^3.
# Winding: counter-clockwise when looking at the face from outside.
# UV: (0,0) = bottom-left of the image as stored in OBJ convention (v up).
#     Metal/Vulkan sample textures with v pointing DOWN -> flip v (v' = 1 - v)
#     either when loading or in the shader. The corner markers in checker.png
#     make a wrong flip obvious.
# Faces use 1-based indices: f v/vt/vn
o cube
v -0.5000 -0.5000 0.5000
v 0.5000 -0.5000 0.5000
v 0.5000 0.5000 0.5000
v -0.5000 0.5000 0.5000
v 0.5000 -0.5000 -0.5000
v -0.5000 -0.5000 -0.5000
v -0.5000 0.5000 -0.5000
v 0.5000 0.5000 -0.5000
v 0.5000 -0.5000 0.5000
v 0.5000 -0.5000 -0.5000
v 0.5000 0.5000 -0.5000
v 0.5000 0.5000 0.5000
v -0.5000 -0.5000 -0.5000
v -0.5000 -0.5000 0.5000
v -0.5000 0.5000 0.5000
v -0.5000 0.5000 -0.5000
v -0.5000 0.5000 0.5000
v 0.5000 0.5000 0.5000
v 0.5000 0.5000 -0.5000
v -0.5000 0.5000 -0.5000
v -0.5000 -0.5000 -0.5000
v 0.5000 -0.5000 -0.5000
v 0.5000 -0.5000 0.5000
v -0.5000 -0.5000 0.5000
vt 0.0000 0.0000
vt 1.0000 0.0000
vt 1.0000 1.0000
vt 0.0000 1.0000
vn 0 0 1
vn 0 0 -1
vn 1 0 0
vn -1 0 0
vn 0 1 0
vn 0 -1 0
# front
f 1/1/1 2/2/1 3/3/1
f 1/1/1 3/3/1 4/4/1
# back
f 5/1/2 6/2/2 7/3/2
f 5/1/2 7/3/2 8/4/2
# right
f 9/1/3 10/2/3 11/3/3
f 9/1/3 11/3/3 12/4/3
# left
f 13/1/4 14/2/4 15/3/4
f 13/1/4 15/3/4 16/4/4
# top
f 17/1/5 18/2/5 19/3/5
f 17/1/5 19/3/5 20/4/5
# bottom
f 21/1/6 22/2/6 23/3/6
f 21/1/6 23/3/6 24/4/6
